From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: issue HFI_FLUSH_ALL on decoder CAPTURE streamoff outside DRC

When stopping a gen1 decoder session in STREAMING state, issuing
HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT on CAPTURE streamoff causes the Huawei SC8280XP video firmware
(qcvss8280.mbn) to stop processing the HFI command queue and time out on all
subsequent session commands.

Match the venus driver's vdec_stop_capture() behaviour on gen1 decoders: issue
HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT only when flushing CAPTURE for a dynamic resolution change
(IRIS_INST_SUB_DRC), and issue HFI_FLUSH_ALL otherwise.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [firmware workaround]
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 7674b47..f00748b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -198,7 +198,17 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_session_stop(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 			if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane))
 				flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_ALL;
 			else if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_CAPTURE(plane))
-				flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT;
+				/*
+				 * Only a resolution change keeps the bitstream queued, so only
+				 * then flush the picture side alone. Any other CAPTURE streamoff
+				 * while streaming (stop, seek) drops the OUTPUT queue right after:
+				 * flush everything, as venus vdec_stop_capture() does. On sc8280xp
+				 * the firmware mostly never completes an HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT sent
+				 * here, and then stops reading the command queue altogether.
+				 */
+				flush_type = inst->sub_state & (IRIS_INST_SUB_DRC |
+								IRIS_INST_SUB_DRC_LAST) ?
+					     HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT : HFI_FLUSH_ALL;
 
 			reinit_completion(&inst->flush_completion);
 
